{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB12459 - MONDO_3582",
  "verbalization": "Belotecan is implicated in the pathogenesis of Hereditary Breast Ovarian Cancer Syndrome through a chain of indications that link it to malignancies associated with this syndrome. The evidence suggests that Belotecan is used to treat Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary, a condition that is associated with Hereditary Breast Ovarian Cancer Syndrome. This connection is further supported by the fact that other drugs, such as Rucaparib and Melphalan, which are also indicated for the same condition, are linked to the syndrome. The shared indication with Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary implies a potential mechanistic link between Belotecan and the syndrome, possibly through the treatment of a common underlying pathology. The evidence suggests that Belotecan may contribute to the development or progression of this syndrome, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
